Z||000000||Spot||03-06-2001||08:25 AM||||Does anyone know what chemical can be used to remove paint from all parts of the Fiero without damaging the plastic. (something that can be placed on the panel and rinsed or easily scraped) I would like to get as close to a raw surface as possible.<P>Thanks||||reg||5
Z||000001||MrPBody||03-06-2001||08:56 AM||||I didn't have much luck with Bulldog paint remover for urethane panels.  I think you have to work on small areas, and I was too impatient.  For me, sanding seems to work best.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tigger||03-06-2001||09:50 AM||||Sand or use a DA.<P>Would not recommend using a paint stripper on a Fiero.  Even thought it could be done, you really risk warping or damaging the panels, especially the urethane facias.||||reg||4
Z||000003||CHOWITT31||03-06-2001||10:57 AM||||Have the car media blasted!<BR>This was the method that I used when I had my Vette painted and the Fiero uses SMC and Urethane panels also.<BR>It is a very safe method for striping the paint off of plastic cars.<BR>Way to risky to try chemical paint removal.<BR>SEE YA||||reg||14
Z||000004||rogergarrison||03-06-2001||11:11 AM||||Ive had many guys try to save money and stripping corvettes with liquid stripper. If theres the slightest opening, pinhole,seam, etc, it will get in and no amount of washing and preping will get it out...until after its painted, then it ruins the paintjob. Any one saying they did it was just extremely lucky.||||reg||1
Z||000005||fropuff||03-06-2001||06:42 PM||||I'd have to say use the DA sander with about a 120 grit.  I used the Bulldog plastic parts chemical stripper, and it worked okay.  It takes a few coats to get it all off, so I'd suggest to use the DA.  It's a lot quicker and works better as well.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||14
Z||000006||fropuff||03-06-2001||06:42 PM||||I'd have to say use the DA sander with about a 120 grit.  I used the Bulldog plastic parts chemical stripper, and it worked okay.  It takes a few coats to get it all off, so I'd suggest to use the DA.  It's a lot quicker and works better as well.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||14
